    <title>Cat FAQ</title>
    <style>
      :root {
        color-scheme: dark;
        --bg: #0b1020;
        --panel: #11172b;
        --panel-2: #171f38;
        --text: #e8ecff;
        --muted: #a9b4d0;
        --accent: #8ab4ff;
        --accent-2: #a78bfa;
        --border: rgba(138, 180, 255, 0.18);
        --shadow: 0 18px 50px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
      }

      * {
        box-sizing: border-box;
      }

      body {
        margin: 0;
        min-height: 100vh;
        font-family: Inter, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
        color: var(--text);
        background:
          radial-gradient(circle at top, rgba(138, 180, 255, 0.16), transparent 32%),
          radial-gradient(circle at 80% 20%, rgba(167, 139, 250, 0.12), transparent 24%),
          var(--bg);
      }

      main {
        max-width: 900px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 64px 20px;
      }

      .hero {
        margin-bottom: 28px;
        padding: 28px;
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: 24px;
        background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04), rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.02));
        box-shadow: var(--shadow);
      }

      .eyebrow {
        margin: 0 0 10px;
        color: var(--accent);
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: 0.14em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
      }

      h1 {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4vw, 3.6rem);
        line-height: 1.05;
      }

      .subtitle {
        margin: 14px 0 0;
        max-width: 62ch;
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 1.05rem;
        line-height: 1.7;
      }

      .faq {
        display: grid;
        gap: 14px;
      }

      .example {
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: 20px;
        background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04), rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.015));
        box-shadow: var(--shadow);
        overflow: hidden;
      }

      .question {
        width: 100%;
        padding: 22px 24px;
        border: 0;
        background: transparent;
        color: var(--text);
        text-align: left;
        font: inherit;
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: space-between;
        gap: 20px;
        cursor: pointer;
      }

      .question:focus-visible {
        outline: 3px solid rgba(138, 180, 255, 0.65);
        outline-offset: -3px;
      }

      .question-title {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: 1.08rem;
        font-weight: 650;
      }

      .chevron {
        flex: none;
        width: 38px;
        height: 38px;
        border-radius: 999px;
        display: grid;
        place-items: center;
        background: rgba(138, 180, 255, 0.12);
        color: var(--accent);
        transition: transform 0.2s ease, background 0.2s ease;
      }

      .details {
        padding: 0 24px 24px;
        color: var(--muted);
        line-height: 1.75;
      }

      .example.open .chevron {
        transform: rotate(180deg);
        background: rgba(167, 139, 250, 0.16);
      }

      .details p {
        margin: 0;
      }

      @media (max-width: 640px) {
        main {
          padding: 24px 14px 40px;
        }

        .hero,
        .question,
        .details {
          padding-left: 18px;
          padding-right: 18px;
        }
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">Cat guide</p>
        <h1 id="faq-title">Frequently asked questions about cats</h1>
        <p class="subtitle">
          A quick, cozy FAQ on what makes cats curious, clever, and very committed to the
          windowsill.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="faq" aria-label="Cat FAQ">
        <div class="example">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="cat-1">
            <h2 class="question-title">Why do cats purr?</h2>
            <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true">⌄</span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" id="cat-1" hidden>
            <p>
              Cats purr when they feel content, but they may also purr to soothe themselves or
              communicate comfort. Think of it as a tiny vibrating signature.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="cat-2">
            <h2 class="question-title">Why do cats knead blankets?</h2>
            <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true">⌄</span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" id="cat-2" hidden>
            <p>
              Kneading is usually a leftover kitten behavior that signals comfort. Many cats do it
              when they are relaxed, especially on soft surfaces and warm laps.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="cat-3">
            <h2 class="question-title">Do cats really like boxes?</h2>
            <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true">⌄</span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" id="cat-3" hidden>
            <p>
              Yes. Boxes offer security, warmth, and a perfect place to investigate the world while
              pretending not to care about it.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="cat-4">
            <h2 class="question-title">How can I keep a cat entertained?</h2>
            <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true">⌄</span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" id="cat-4" hidden>
            <p>
              Use interactive toys, scratching posts, climbing spaces, and short play sessions.
              Variety matters, because cats appreciate novelty almost as much as routine.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <script>
      document.querySelectorAll(".example").forEach((item) => {
        const button = item.querySelector(".question");
        const details = item.querySelector(".details");

        button.addEventListener("click", () => {
          const isOpen = button.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true";
          button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(!isOpen));
          details.hidden = isOpen;
          item.classList.toggle("open", !isOpen);
        });
      });
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
