          windowsill.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="faq" aria-label="Cat FAQ">
        <div class="example">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="cat-1">
            <span class="question-title">Why do cats purr?</span>
            <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true">⌄</span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" id="cat-1" hidden>
            <p>
              Cats purr when they feel content, but they may also purr to soothe themselves or
              communicate comfort. Think of it as a tiny vibrating signature.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="cat-2">
            <span class="question-title">Why do cats knead blankets?</span>
            <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true">⌄</span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" id="cat-2" hidden>
            <p>
              Kneading is usually a leftover kitten behavior that signals comfort. Many cats do it
              when they are relaxed, especially on soft surfaces and warm laps.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="cat-3">
            <span class="question-title">Do cats really like boxes?</span>
            <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true">⌄</span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" id="cat-3" hidden>
            <p>
              Yes. Boxes offer security, warmth, and a perfect place to investigate the world while
              pretending not to care about it.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="cat-4">
            <span class="question-title">How can I keep a cat entertained?</span>
            <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true">⌄</span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" id="cat-4" hidden>
            <p>
              Use interactive toys, scratching posts, climbing spaces, and short play sessions.
              Variety matters, because cats appreciate novelty almost as much as routine.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <script>
      document.querySelectorAll(".example").forEach((item) => {
        const button = item.querySelector(".question");
        const details = item.querySelector(".details");

